From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 15:30:37 +0200
Subject: dt-bindings: net: dsa: lantiq,gswip: add the Intel xRX500 switch
 macros

The two switch macros of the Intel xRX500 SoC family run a GSWIP-3.0
switch core: the register block the models already described here run, at
the same offsets, with further blocks above it. Two of those blocks are
ones the earlier models place in regions of their own, the MDIO master and
the per-port link registers, so on this generation a single region covers
the switch core, the macro's top block and the packet MAC that faces the
SoC's queue manager. The MDIO bus and the firmware loader for the
integrated PHYs reach their registers through that region, so neither is a
device of its own and neither takes a region or a syscon of its own.

Describe that. Two compatibles, one per macro, because the macro that
carries the external port has a different port count and a different set
of per-port blocks. One region rather than three. A firmware loader that
takes the image name from the device tree, and whose children's offsets
are inside the switch region rather than in the reset control unit. And
dma-noncoherent, which is not decoration here: the PHY cores fetch their
firmware outside the coherence domain the platform sets up, so the staged
image has to be written back before they are released, and a driver that
is told the switch is coherent cannot do that.

Every constraint that was unconditional becomes conditional on the model,
so nothing changes for the models already described.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

